course: dictionary
lesson: 5031
title: Inherit: passed down to you
level: primary-5
stars: 3
explain: To inherit something is to receive it from someone who came before you. Sometimes that means money, a house or a thing that belonged to someone else. Sometimes it means a feature, like the colour of your eyes, that you got from your parents.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «When close relatives have babies together, inherited illnesses become more common.» Relatives are family, and illnesses are things that make you ill, so inherited illnesses must be illnesses passed down in families. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it.
explain: Inherit can also mean to take over a job or a problem that someone leaves behind. «Some dams have been repaired for hundreds of years by family after family of beavers, each one fixing the dam it inherited.» Each beaver takes over a dam from the beaver before, and fixes it.
fact: To inherit means to receive something from someone who came before you.
fact: You can inherit money, a house, or a feature such as hair shape, which comes from your family.
fact: «Inherited» means passed down, often from parents through genes.
fact: «Cystic fibrosis» is an inherited condition, which means it is passed down from parents.
fact: To inherit a problem or job means to take it over from someone before you.
exercise: «Some dams have been repaired for hundreds of years by family after family of beavers, each one fixing the dam it inherited.» What does inherited mean here? | Painted it blue | Built it from brand-new sticks | Ate it for lunch | *Took it over from the beavers before
exercise: «Round follicles grow straight hair, and hair shape is inherited from your family.» What does inherited mean? | Caused by the weather | *Passed down to you from your family | Cut by a hairdresser | Chosen by you each morning
exercise: «Cystic fibrosis is an inherited condition, and it is not catching.» Find and copy the word that means spreads from person to person. | inherited | *catching | lungs | sticky
test: If you inherit blue eyes, what have you got? | *Eye colour passed down to you from your parents | Eyes that change colour every day | A cousin's eyes for a week | A new pair of glasses
test: «The youngest son inherited a cat.» What does this tell you? | He lost the cat in the park | He drew a picture of a cat | He bought a cat from a shop | *He received the cat from someone who had it before him
exam: Which sentence uses inherit to mean take over a job or problem left by someone before you? | He inherited a bike for his birthday from the shop | *The new manager inherited a messy office and an unfinished report from the last boss | She inherited blue eyes from her dad | They inherited a sunny afternoon at the beach
